{"files": [{"id": 17387882, "name": "spikeAndBehavioralData.zip", "size": 8862131563, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/17387882", "supplied_md5": "e7b684888dfdc350e5b6a4baf04221e0", "computed_md5": "e7b684888dfdc350e5b6a4baf04221e0", "mimetype": "application/zip"}, {"id": 17388203, "name": "fig1_BehavAndRec.jpg", "size": 750728, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/17388203", "supplied_md5": "76f134605b406a95a309caaefaafa657", "computed_md5": "76f134605b406a95a309caaefaafa657", "mimetype": "image/jpeg"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 6033494, "full_name": "Nick Steinmetz", "first_name": "Nick", "last_name": "Steinmetz", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Nick_Steinmetz", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 6179794, "full_name": "Peter Zatka-Haas", "first_name": "Peter", "last_name": "Zatka-Haas", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 6778853, "full_name": "Matteo Carandini", "first_name": "Matteo", "last_name": "Carandini", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Matteo_Carandini", "orcid_id": "0000-0003-4880-7682"}, {"id": 6766349, "full_name": "Kenneth Harris", "first_name": "Kenneth", "last_name": "Harris", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Kenneth_Harris", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Dataset_from_Steinmetz_et_al_2019/9598406", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<b>Main dataset from Steinmetz et al. 2019. </b><div><br></div><div><div><i>Companion code located at </i><a href=\"https://github.com/nsteinme/steinmetz-et-al-2019\">https://github.com/nsteinme/steinmetz-et-al-2019</a><i>.</i></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><i>Raw behavioral movies located here: </i><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9702302\">https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9702302</a></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><i>Raw local field potential data located here: </i><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9727895\">https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9727895</a></div></div><div><br></div><div><i>Data also accessible via Open Neurophysiology Environment (</i><a href=\"https://figshare.com/articles/steinmetz/9974357\">https://figshare.com/articles/steinmetz/9974357</a><i>) and in Neurodata Without Borders format (</i><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.11274968\">https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.11274968</a><i>). </i></div><div><br></div><div>This dataset contains both spiking and behavioral data. </div><div><br></div><div><div>Spiking data is provided after spike sorting.</div></div><div><br></div><div>Behavioral data includes wheel movements, pupil area and position, stimulus information, choice information. </div><div><br></div><div>Detailed information about the files provided can be found here: <a href=\"https://github.com/nsteinme/steinmetz-et-al-2019/wiki/data-files\">https://github.com/nsteinme/steinmetz-et-al-2019/wiki/data-files</a></div><div><br></div><div><div>When extracting the zip file provided here, you will get \"allData.tar\", then extract that tar file to get individual .tar files for each recording, and then extract each of these. It is convenient to do this last step using WinRAR in Windows by selecting all, right-clicking on one of them, and choosing \"extract each to separate folder\". <br></div></div><div><br></div>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 2, "status": "public", "size": 8862882291, "created_date": "2019-08-25T19:08:27Z", "modified_date": "2023-05-30T11:31:14Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["neuropixels", "vision", "behavior", "Neuroscience", "Animal Neurobiology"], "keywords": ["neuropixels", "vision", "behavior", "Neuroscience", "Animal Neurobiology"], "categories": [{"id": 24748, "title": "Neurosciences no